F87FF]links-resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-resolver: add a Rust three-way links/*.json index merge and wire a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]second semantic resolver into both rebase-repair paths so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]distinct-reader conflicts stop pausing agents.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Immutable link-event contract and reducer in Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]event-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]event-contract: define content-addressed link-event files, canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serialization, operation identity, and a deterministic event-set reducer[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in sase-core with Python bindings, beside the landed publication-policy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]module.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable operation identity in the link outbox[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]outbox-identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after event-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]outbox-identity: give every queued link mutation a full-strength [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operation id, stop count-collapsing distinct operations, and define [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retirement semantics that compose with the per-root publication retry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Automatic link writes publish as events through the machine [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]lane[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]event-publisher[dim] · [dim][/dim]after outbox-identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]event-publisher: behind a new beta flag, automatic writers enqueue [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]events instead of dirtying agent sidecar clones, and a serialized [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-project publisher batches them into the hidden host-owned clones [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the existing commit choke point so the sase-yh retry ledger owns[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]push retry.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Readers, projections, and maintenance consume reduced events[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]event-readers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after event-contract, outbox-identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]event-readers: aggregate rebuilds, link list/doctor, managed Markdown [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocks, and rename handling read reduced events overlaid with pending [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]outbox operations, with alias events replacing event-path rewrites.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fence, import legacy indexes, and cut over[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]cutover-import[dim] · [dim][/dim]after links-resolver, event-publisher, event-readers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cutover-import: one-shot deterministic import of frozen legacy indexes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into baseline events, flag enablement and removal, read-only legacy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]indexes, doctor guardrails, and re-pointing the publication retry lane's[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy-index discovery at the event lane.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Multi-clone acceptance suite and conflict-free guarantee[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cutover-import[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: end-to-end suite with independent clones and two simulated [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machines proving zero link-metadata merge pauses, no lost or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]double-counted operations, retry-ledger-driven recovery at every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publication boundary, and clean crash recovery.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-yy","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-yy.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-yy.1"},"source_run_id":"run-ad97881acc67e77057301766fdd58ff2","started_at":"2026-09-09T15:50:07.617241+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"fe7b67f2923f39f839496dc44e74c9f2d59fa490b5b8a1a6187b74208e7b8788","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-yy.4/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"0f42818faabd67cd03e0edfeff432814cfd679d3886f56bcc224dfd137b9abe9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-yy.4/meta.json","size_bytes":637},"prompt":{"digest":"156cda30f7c0568675453d1e8b000106c475d0b0e5f879225013ee08c7582f2f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-yy.4/prompt.md","size_bytes":146},"state":{"digest":"f91cd7c00936884e04c9729ad4a6d5f7a81a5fae99b756ffd2353913d38097f4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-yy.4/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-yy.4","local_name":"sase-yy.4","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-yy","agent_clan_generation":"20260909114934","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-yy.4","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-yy","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-yy.4","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-ae14ad004dd1834db3ce255f36f12921","started_at":"20260909114937","state":"waiting"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"